#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115071 :question/id #uuid "f2c7cfd3-da43-5208-bd0e-21692357fabe" :question/math-academy-id "e-4712" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=1, \\\\ 4x+ky &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n\n\n$$\nM= \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{array} \\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=1 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673977 :question-generator/id #uuid "e083cdd9-caa3-54b0-9d5e-a4fa6ea10ea4" :question-generator/script "generators/4b/4b1dc96d53691c1e5d73bda23fa8a419c1ca37c02f592bebce091e68f48e79a2/17592186115242.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3248af5c-24d6-51a0-a62b-8d5ab0e0e782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300213} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed5f31b-5757-56ca-ac90-622019b8d7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300447} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3ca3f5-57b3-5b3c-b6b4-0772e9be135c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300503} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2681ec-b8ae-51dc-9094-2e2bcadf6d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300522} {:answer/id #uuid "fad186f0-c1c8-5bcc-8cc3-09b1f4f1ed49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ed5f31b-5757-56ca-ac90-622019b8d7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300447} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bc72922-bebc-50a1-a8ff-483d8fbfcfc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301729}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a9a3feb-6c16-50e8-885d-ee5cd242ab95" :question/math-academy-id "q-32246" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y &=12 \\\\ x+ky &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4-3k & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+ky &=4 \\\\ (4-3k)y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{4}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{4}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425939} {:answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} {:answer/id #uuid "545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425942} {:answer/id #uuid "684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425943} {:answer/id #uuid "9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a07998-8f4c-5e30-bdee-b2acbf389fbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113923}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84cf8820-fa64-5d50-9d9c-d3a9404788a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42059" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=1 \\\\ 6x+(k+3)y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=1 \\\\ (k-6)y &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=-8,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188d8234-d927-5fa4-9649-52a3600a14ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263232} {:answer/id #uuid "59917889-7526-5cea-90f8-6ed9b5d31888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263771} {:answer/id #uuid "84ec393a-992f-55d2-9044-1e362627ed1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264142} {:answer/id #uuid "9556b060-0b9f-5486-b05c-79753916db1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264279} {:answer/id #uuid "c483c739-bc7d-5f47-8dbf-09da12b3a0b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "188d8234-d927-5fa4-9649-52a3600a14ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263232} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c23e17f-c925-52e8-86bd-0f648e063de0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265388}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d3ed27b-d876-58c6-8a51-55f4b36743e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-131726" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y &=1 \\\\ 6x+(k+9)y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+13 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y &=1 \\\\ (k+13)y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-13,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-13.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4e76fd-e1c6-5cbe-93b0-49387b6d03cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263361} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f1c78c-35e7-5dc3-a4ea-917746946f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264698} {:answer/id #uuid "cad2e0cc-59d8-5847-8c17-7f7022f7428b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264775} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd34857-39b4-5a84-88c6-46284b56c129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264929} {:answer/id #uuid "f74d0318-2803-55b8-bb5b-49c8150dea17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f74d0318-2803-55b8-bb5b-49c8150dea17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265163} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ce296a-26b4-5d5b-bab5-71101c246341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265471}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e7e4e8f-70c3-5d1c-92c5-d1d6f120ba7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-131727" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-1 \\\\ 4x+3ky &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3k+12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-1 \\\\ (3k+12)y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e3a6e2e-1b7a-5ad1-b366-2deecae63253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264216} {:answer/id #uuid "96b3aa58-5c89-5f3c-896e-547bdfeef87c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264291} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0fed83-26f2-58cf-9e61-edca1345442b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264336} {:answer/id #uuid "bedfa238-a1cb-50f4-b26d-08ac9994d923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264662} {:answer/id #uuid "cffb3874-d3c5-58d9-9efc-875fe9730f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96b3aa58-5c89-5f3c-896e-547bdfeef87c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264291} :answer-field/id #uuid "567ae966-e7d1-5296-a3f6-661d2e59d117" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265397}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5288d9bb-0110-5357-979f-882b0ee060b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-131728" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y &=-2 \\\\ -3x+(3k+15)y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3k+3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y &=-2 \\\\ (3k+3)y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-1,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427da7e5-15ac-51bd-a759-d90b6c65d454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263588} {:answer/id #uuid "538a47b2-6a0b-5a53-99e0-b4e09df09626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263720} {:answer/id #uuid "7f383d71-c4b1-501b-823d-dfdddaac22d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264099} {:answer/id #uuid "b60949ed-65e4-5904-90e9-755392f2794a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264578} {:answer/id #uuid "d7266032-5cfb-59d1-b694-4b3ac335232b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b60949ed-65e4-5904-90e9-755392f2794a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264578} :answer-field/id #uuid "446ceb46-6d4a-51ab-82b3-1f055fd41555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49ba50cf-14b7-5be4-8660-2e096dc4c172" :question/math-academy-id "q-131729" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+7y &=6 \\\\ x+ky &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 1 & k & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 1 & k & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2k+7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+ky &=-3 \\\\ (2k+7)y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=-\\frac{7}{2},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=-3.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=-\\frac{7}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5280ce29-a009-5d89-b11c-32a91956f88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263711} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cf5fce-3112-5b03-8cf3-0d4a08494133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264442} {:answer/id #uuid "bac8e055-43dd-52ec-b2ee-c1af2bc589d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264621} {:answer/id #uuid "bf50ed27-034a-525d-8d4e-b76acf4ead2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264666} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c3e1a0-f525-5859-8a97-2dbc90d7ad24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5280ce29-a009-5d89-b11c-32a91956f88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263711} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe108dd5-5b35-596c-94e7-349c53f9ba7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87026642-3a4d-5af1-8cd6-01d366fc76fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-131731" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+6y &=-4 \\\\ 5x+(k-6)y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & k-6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & k-6 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+6y &=-4 \\\\ (k+9)y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=-9,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y.$ So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $-2x+6y=-4.$  \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=-9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eefeb35-a93a-5693-8a54-a335560cde62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 1759