equations above must be false.\n\nNow if $k=-2$, then the second equation is $0=-2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when  $k=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39edf270-ef24-52e6-8a06-10a72874478d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300241} {:answer/id #uuid "441122b0-3b95-5e4c-ad49-ebd17ab5fd1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300297} {:answer/id #uuid "7951ba97-6d77-594c-84f6-7b1ce6a00426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300560} {:answer/id #uuid "8713309c-6e3b-5cbf-9236-a21b2e8d5efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300642} {:answer/id #uuid "99ccc30d-db87-5ff3-b366-54bc530fc04c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39edf270-ef24-52e6-8a06-10a72874478d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300241} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a94e5ac-1c4c-5f66-9534-54809e136ec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301608}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5f8dda9-f72e-566e-91bc-44ecdce08b8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32331" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y &=2 \\\\ 8x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y &=2 \\\\ (k-2)y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b9a3770-af37-58af-91e7-3430fd2463b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343154} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae964-c567-5585-ab23-7241fb114732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343221} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3da90-4b17-5b45-af78-2746f79a0b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343724} {:answer/id #uuid "ad97781e-f202-56a0-803a-f17ee1a49ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343764} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344664}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593" :question/math-academy-id "q-74646" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 2x+(k+1)y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ (k-7)y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30949865-bcb4-5324-b20a-5013ed16ed8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342643} {:answer/id #uuid "b02857e6-f7e6-504c-84a4-ca08044eec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343786} {:answer/id #uuid "bd377e49-f3f5-59d7-82a4-fcccc36aefd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343902} {:answer/id #uuid "cffbe52d-faab-5e8d-a8c2-edecdb561a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344066} {:answer/id #uuid "d763087a-bc9a-5f66-ac0e-8fa93b6ecd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffbe52d-faab-5e8d-a8c2-edecdb561a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344066} :answer-field/id #uuid "78098d80-b356-5405-a056-ca928a0838fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdfa86e8-f2dc-5d19-9144-98ae43ab2ede" :question/math-academy-id "q-74688" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ 3x+2ky &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2k & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2k & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2k-6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ (2k-6)y &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=3,$ then the second equation is $0=10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba1e46b-dcb4-5f9e-b60f-f807d3ae1d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342339} {:answer/id #uuid "47f4259f-5c12-50a0-8a37-001fbf58b6db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342833} {:answer/id #uuid "761008e6-93b4-567d-8e13-46b3d3b90948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759