id "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557412} {:answer/id #uuid "7876e850-f579-5b07-8b9c-174d601fcc57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557425} {:answer/id #uuid "86b4dd02-2b53-599b-a39f-7cdb9621c84d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557426} {:answer/id #uuid "8d82f745-e687-53bf-a943-5f5c160a27c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557429} {:answer/id #uuid "90469b9f-cd36-5eb9-a240-2e5bd047b529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557412} :answer-field/id #uuid "b669bb3f-c7dc-5f8f-b577-73556f01d6a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557435}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4508cab0-6e88-59d6-a9c3-7b9fc61a9c9d" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ 3x+ky &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ (k+6)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58b63595-07c3-5725-80e1-8d68eb1d1eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557420} {:answer/id #uuid "58f14b39-9200-54eb-8f1e-3dda0f24757d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557421} {:answer/id #uuid "60a6d9bd-3eb0-5fbb-8b4c-3b367438cadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557424} {:answer/id #uuid "87e3b172-ceb3-5955-b7d5-9979995635ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557427} {:answer/id #uuid "bea126fd-72a5-56d7-8f24-ee9beadcdf63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58b63595-07c3-5725-80e1-8d68eb1d1eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557420} :answer-field/id #uuid "d43ac781-bcce-57c0-9a91-14ff48ccf057" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557441}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "550c7cdf-5810-56e4-b192-4674132b8147" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-4 \\\\ 2x+ky &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & k & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & k & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-4 \\\\ (k+6)y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040900c0-cbe2-5a3b-bf63-00c6502b1713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557410} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce26fa4-9b16-5f35-94ea-df9965919477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557413} {:answer/id #uuid "895f3ba6-7e73-5ee1-88ee-96b78cf55a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557428} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8a51e6-cd68-5ca8-bf4b-3b66c24eddc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557431} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b4341b-24d7-5601-bee0-2b97f2a49be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "040900c0-cbe2-5a3b-bf63-00c6502b1713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557410} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bbf5c12-3409-5553-9dd1-d59b687d99b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557423}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4f00ddd-faa4-5195-9569-dbec2d0e2e6c" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "242bb709-6a59-58a9-96b4-f4cec6fd4c01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186579739} {:answer/id #uuid "57e256eb-a9dc-540d-80d5-ee1ba8faf497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186579824} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9647eb-8180-5595-b3d8-c540726b4f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186579913} {:answer/id #uuid "f562c61b-fc92-5d40-9174-8d634e874557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580100} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b5bc8a-d9e4-562d-93da-99a50c6386f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57e256eb-a9dc-540d-80d5-ee1ba8faf497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186579824} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc64a0ef-bd09-50d3-bf4e-445a2a65aed6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580210}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "113efc76-e9d2-549d-b33e-b8de028f7ba5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74691" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=4 \\\\ -3x+ky &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & k & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & k & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & k-3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=4 \\\\ (k-3)y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=3,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$,. So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $2x+2y=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d2288-8ec8-5e6d-a4d8-095077c48bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673946} {:answer/id #uuid "6aee5c58-e2b4-5f01-b8e0-82c1d4d6fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673957} {:answer/id #uuid "c538572d-fdb5-5531-91f3-68a9da295fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673971} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfaa07e-0f58-59c2-893c-21f92247653a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673974} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4de40d-50a1-5d55-88c4-b30849d049d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c538572d-fdb5-5531-91f3-68a9da295fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673971} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f58f00-49ce-5578-a2fd-f96ec70eeb0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a93d453-0c6e-55ff-bedb-71deca93f8cf" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ 2x+ky &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & k & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & k & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & k+8 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ (k+8)y &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-8,$ then the second equation is $0=10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efe90b4-562a-5953-a6a1-cc05ec46980b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673943} {:answer/id #uuid "67823551-800c-5cf7-948d-beb12cd02bf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673955} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8fa752-119c-51a0-b6e2-66d7985075e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673963} {:answer/id #uuid "98c304e3-a115-5ace-9fab-90964849999e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673965} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f936e8-86b0-5f40-9374-4f0caee0a413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c304e3-a115-5ace-9fab-90964849999e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673965} :answer-field/id #uuid "65831a37-c7e4-528e-a925-5b3e241729ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673954}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81014666-3726-55af-9dd0-135ed4dcb4b9" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ -2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & k-4 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ (k-4)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=4,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a84b70-9245-5d97-a4d9-55045854331f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673947} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9d77cc-bf23-57d7-922e-1fb20688eb3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673948} {:answer/id #uuid "4116de3c-ec2b-537f-a54c-e14f8c2d7871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673952} {:answer/id #uuid "879ad630-9d2f-568c-8679-659f0ddc56fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673962} {:answer/id #uuid "c3161b92-ed93-588e-b5d8-221d41adb4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25a84b70-9245-5d97-a4d9-55045854331f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673947} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee32c4a-a732-5943-9bdb-dec719ab233a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ed86d41-824a-5162-a0b1-66e0498bfd9d" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ 3x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & k+12 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ (k+12)y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-12,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044d5930-e9c2-5606-a6c3-a9b35fdcaf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673942} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb6ed59-3b1b-5e76-8348-af3553644638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673944} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb5c6d1-171c-5fac-96b5-ed6bc2cb9d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673951} {:answer/id #uuid "483b361a-fa4f-569e-9ee3-9a27510e751b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673953} {:answer/id #uuid "f0daf48f-38d9-5ace-b